MONAI Consortium, https://github.com/Project-MONAI/MONAI

Changes by this project (2026-11-08):
- Move architecture into merit_covid.models.unetrpp, split modules, format
  code and explain tensor dimensions; retain upstream parameter names.
- Replace SegmentationNetwork with torch.nn.Module; omit nnU-Net trainer,
  sliding-window inference framework and their unrelated dependencies.
- Use torch.nn.init.trunc_normal_ instead of timm's equivalent initializer;
  use einops directly; omit unused custom LayerNorm and Fourier modules.
- Supply consistent default dimensions (upstream expects dims explicitly);
  forward in_channels to the patch stem (upstream omitted this argument).
- Derive encoder/decoder token counts and final feature shape from an
  explicitly declared fixed img_size. The original (64,128,128) produces
  the original constants. Smaller configured grids/channels are test
  adaptations, not published experimental settings.
- Validate shapes, channel/head/group compatibility and invalid inputs.
- Add a separate binary master-slice output adapter with no input transform.
- Add model-only YAML, synthetic tests, provenance and Vietnamese docs.
- Add opt-in preserve_z to model.py and encoder.py for the separate paper-derived
  MERIT model: (1,4,4) stem and (1,2,2) down/up strides. Default False retains
  the original Synapse topology and state-dict shapes.

No EPA equations, shared E/F projection, additive decoder skips, residual
paths or segmentation-head activations were changed. Upstream Synapse has
one residual conv block per transformer (the Lung variant differs); this
integration intentionally uses the Synapse variant throughout. Deep
supervision returns the same three resolutions; no automatic upsampling.

No dataset/preprocessing/split changes, training, pretrained weights,
checkpoint downloads or experimental model results are included.
